  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a poster who typed an emoji, I want to be told before sending and offered a matching smiley, so that HFR does not cut my message.\n\n### Scope\n\nComposer highlights refused characters and offers the LOT-096 (#188) suggestions in one tap.\n\n- Module: App · Difficulty: easy · Priority: medium · post-MVP\n- Implements: FEAT-012 (#156)\n- Absorbs: FEAT-012\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master`): none (new); Q-3 decision\n- Spec: `docs/features/FEAT-012.md` (feature spec, ADR 0011 §2; write it first if absent, crediting Bybifok) plus a short `docs/lots/LOT-151-*.md` pointing to it\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-096 (#188)\n- LOT-084 (#176)\n- LOT-104 (#195)\n\n### Blocked by\n\ndependencies not done: LOT-096 (#188), LOT-084 (#176), LOT-104 (#195)\n\n### Feature umbrella\n\n- Implements FEAT-012 (#156), proposed by Bybifok (credit in the spec, PR and CREDITS.md). Other lots of this feature: LOT-096 (#188); **this lot is the last one: its PR also says `Closes #156`**.\n\nFEAT issues (#145–#165) are umbrellas and are never claimed: claim this lot's issue; the PR says `Closes #<this issue>` and `Refs #<FEAT issue>`.\n\n### Model\n\nSonnet → Opus (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- CAP-N3 (#171): Post with a BMP emoji (e.g. U+2764) and with a variation selector (U+FE0F): kept, replaced or truncated?\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Send stays disabled while refused characters remain; replacement keeps the rest of the text intact.\n- [ ] View logic lives in `@Observable @MainActor` models tested with Swift Testing in `App/SwiftHFRTests/`; each new test is shown to fail without the change.\n- [ ] `xcodebuild build test` green on the iPhone 18 Pro and an iPad simulator (iOS 27.0), and the `App build + tests` CI job green.\n- [ ] UI strings in French; light, dark and Dynamic Type XL checked; no new dependency; no HFR fact without a source (legacy file:line or fixture).\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).",
